Captured with `git log --date=iso` in this repository, with the author name and
email replaced. 29 commits.

This is the repro a tester reported against v0.3.1: `git log` was wrapped (it
had been rtk's territory until v0.3.1 made toktrim standalone, and the query
list had never needed to classify it), so it went through head/tail truncation
and lost 18 of 29 commits. The dedup window separately suppressed 18 identical
`Author:` lines, so even surviving commits were missing their author. The whole
output must now come through untouched.
